Connecting the vendor WiFi driver Realtek (drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8192cd).

As with the Ethernet driver, the code is not included in the patch: it is an overlay in
target/linux/rtkmipsel/files/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8192cd/. It was assembled
from the vendor Realtek SDK v3.4.14b source in the D-Link DIR-842E GPL archive. The patch
only needs to expose that directory to the kernel build system, hence the two lines.


This is a literal analogue of the patch 950-rtk_add_rtl8192cd_wifi_support.patch from the fork
openwrt-AC10, with one difference: for AC10 the driver is assembled inside the mac80211 package
(backports), so there is a prefix CPTCFG_; we collect kernels in the tree, so CONFIG_.
The context of both files in 4.14 coincided with the version AC10 verbatim - the same three lines
source in realtek/Kconfig and the same four obj- in realtek/Makefile.

The patch was generated from the Linux 4.14.275 reference tree rather than edited by
hand, so its context matches that source revision.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/Kconfig
@@ -14,5 +14,6 @@
 source "drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl818x/Kconfig"
 source "drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtlwifi/Kconfig"
 source "drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8xxxu/Kconfig"
+source "drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8192cd/Kconfig"
 
 endif # WLAN_VENDOR_REALTEK
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/Makefile
@@ -6,4 +6,5 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_RTL8187)		+= rtl818x/
 obj-$(CONFIG_RTLWIFI)		+= rtlwifi/
 obj-$(CONFIG_RTL8XXXU)		+= rtl8xxxu/
+obj-$(CONFIG_RTL8192CD)		+= rtl8192cd/
 
